  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb",
  "gloss": "arousal; calling to attention; evocation",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "arousing; calling to attention; evoking (interest, awareness, opinion)",
      "explanation": "The act of bringing something to public attention or drawing out a feeling, awareness, or memory. Used in formal contexts about opinion, concern, or interest."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "28817_kanki_ex1",
      "japanese": "{注意|ちゅうい}を{喚起|かんき}する。",
      "english": "To call attention to something.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "28817_kanki_ex2",
      "japanese": "{世論|よろん}の{喚起|かんき}を{目的|もくてき}とした{記事|きじ}だ。",
      "english": "It is an article aimed at arousing public opinion.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "28817_kanki_ex3",
      "japanese": "{環境問題|かんきょうもんだい}への{関心|かんしん}を{喚起|かんき}するための{講演会|こうえんかい}が{開|ひら}かれた。",
      "english": "A lecture was held to raise interest in environmental issues.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Formal, written register. Typically appears with abstract objects like {注意|ちゅうい}, {関心|かんしん}, {興味|きょうみ}, {世論|よろん}, {記憶|きおく}. Common in news and academic writing.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {注意|ちゅうい}{喚起|かんき}: a warning; calling attention to a danger\n- {関心|かんしん}を{喚起|かんき}する: to arouse interest\n- {興味|きょうみ}を{喚起|かんき}する: to spark interest\n- {世論|よろん}を{喚起|かんき}する: to mobilize public opinion\n- {記憶|きおく}を{喚起|かんき}する: to bring back memories\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {呼|よ}び{起|お}こす: to evoke; to call up — more concrete and conversational\n- {引|ひ}き{起|お}こす: to cause; to bring about — focuses on causing an event, not awareness",
